B.bRo=new A.kX("update_agenda","Manage your agenda \u2014 what you intend to do, as opposed to what you know (that goes to update_memory). Create one the moment you take on a task or commitment: the human asks you to prepare, find, or do something; you promise to act at a certain moment (`act_at` \u2014 when that moment arrives, you act on your own initiative); or you are working through something with steps worth tracking. Keep it alive as things progress \u2014 mark steps done as you go, complete or cancel when finished \u2014 so the agenda always reflects where you really are. There can be at most ONE current agenda without `act_at` (your single present focus); any number of agendas WITH `act_at`. If a passive agenda already exists, finish or cancel it first, or merge the new intent into its steps. Address an agenda by its `label`. Actions: `create` (label + goal, optional act_at, optional steps), `edit` (goal and/or act_at), `add_step`, `step` (mark an ordinal done/cancelled, optional result), `complete`, `cancel`.",B.bB4,!1,!0,!1,B.jD)
